ok - attach: a preserved head is restored from its bundle onto its own branch
ok - attach: a home-relative bundle restores its head and branch from the invocation directory
ok - attach: an existing branch at the preserved head is checked out, never re-cut
ok - attach: every refusal stops before the copy, the record, or any branch is touched
ok - attach: a branch origin moved past the preserved head refuses without creating it
ok - attach: origin is asked for the exact branch, so a narrow fetch refspec cannot hide another head
ok - attach: a project with no origin attaches a head it already holds
ok - attach: a failure after the checkout puts the copy back and drops only the branch it created, so a retry attaches
ok - attach: a failure after the checkout keeps a branch that existed before the attach
